 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "An internal current limit holds the output current down under a short, and a thermal-overload circuit shuts the regulator off when the die overheats. Together they make the part close to immune from overload damage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "External parts",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The regulator needs no external components to work. Its electrical figures are specified with a 0.33 µF capacitor on the input and a 0.1 µF capacitor on the output, each to common."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Suited to regulating locally on each board rather than from one shared supply. The output can drive an external series pass transistor for a negative regulator of higher current. Compared with a Zener diode and resistor, output impedance is about 100 times lower and bias current is lower."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Headroom",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Dropout is 1.7 V typical at 40 mA and 25 °C. The −5 V parts are specified from −7 V to −20 V in, the −12 V parts from −14.5 V to −27 V, and the −15 V parts from −17.5 V to −30 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "SOIC input pins",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "In the D package the four INPUT pins (2, 3, 6, 7) are one node inside; COMMON is pin 5 alone, and pins 4 and 8 are unconnected."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The AC suffix is the 5% output tolerance grade, the C suffix the 10% grade. Both are rated for a 0 to 125 °C junction."
  },
  {
   "topic": "LP lead forms",
   "page": 12,
   "text": "Straight leads come in bulk packs only; formed leads come on tape and reel or in ammo packs. Not every part is offered in every combination of lead form and packing."
  }
 ],
